<title>FRANCE: EU fixed wheat taxes and barley refunds unchanged.</title>
<headline>EU fixed wheat taxes and barley refunds unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday left standing export taxes for wheat and standing refunds for barley unchanged, grain officials said.</p>
<p>The latest standing soft wheat export tax is six Ecus per tonne.  </p>
<p>Refunds for rye exports were also unchanged.</p>
<p>Fixed export taxes and refunds are available each day through an alternative bidding system to the main tender.</p>
<p>Latest taxes are as follows (Ecus per tonne)-</p>
<p>    Durum wheat grain	    15.00</p>
<p>    Soft wheat grain		6.00</p>
<p>    Durum wheat flour	    22.50</p>
<p>    Soft wheat flour		8.50</p>
<p>    Durum semolina		 22.50</p>
<p>    Soft wheat semolina	   8.50</p>
<p>------</p>
<p>Latest refunds are as follows.</p>
<p>Barley to Switzerland/</p>
<p>	     Liechtenstein	  2.00</p>
<p>    Barley to elsewhere	   0.00</p>
<p>Rye to Switzerland/</p>
<p>	     Liechtenstein	 13.00</p>
<p>    Rye to elsewhere		0.00</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
